  "caveats": [
    "Still strictly sequential: one write in flight, so the advisory lock is never contended.",
    "batchApplies defaults on and engages only for a run that canBatch accepts; the excluded cases still write one operation per transaction. The cells here force the flag either way so the comparison is explicit.",
    "Batching makes a job's writes atomic where they were previously committed one at a time, which is a semantic change beyond performance and is called out in the writeup."
  ]
